WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.137
After low rah adapters are attached, measure the trainable parameter count instead of simply assuming the configuration

00:00:08.137 --> 00:00:14.517
is lightweight. The code counts parameters whose requires grad flag is true, counts the total parameters,

00:00:14.517 --> 00:00:17.312
and calculates the trainable percentage.

00:00:17.312 --> 00:00:20.312
This is a useful verification step.

00:00:20.312 --> 00:00:27.512
A low rah configuration only helps if it targets the intended modules and leaves the expected fraction of the base model

00:00:27.512 --> 00:00:28.515
frozen.
